completion_raw:
There are several ways to terminate a C program in C, you can use the exit() function to terminate a program. The exit() function takes an integer argument that represents the exit status of the program. Here is an example:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, world!\n");
    exit(0);
    return 0;
}
```

In this example, the program prints "Hello, world!" to the console and then terminates with an exit status of 0.

